WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:02.820
Speaker 1: Let's talk a little bit about the
COVID pandemic.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.880
We may be approaching what what might be the
first?

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:07.880
So what wave?

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.500
And I'm not the person who came up with that.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.070
There's a good Atlantic article that uses
that term.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:20.179
We had the original wave, we had Delta, we
had our McCrum, and we may be getting to the

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:21.179
first.

00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:26.320
So what wave where most people may just not
do anything differently?

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.149
We just don't know.

00:00:28.149 --> 00:00:33.980
But pandemic fatigue aside, it's starting
to look like something may be happening.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.370
So a few headlines.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:42.050
Philadelphia is restoring indoor mask mandates
as cases rise, we've gotten away from almost

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.690
any mask mandates.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:44.690
Yes.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:49.289
Transportation federally, although that may
go away April 18th, although it may not now

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:52.480
that the numbers are starting to rise in some
places.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:57.489
Again, medical facilities and I think most
states are, I don't I don't even remember

00:00:57.489 --> 00:00:58.489
if that's federal.

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:02.030
In most places, you go to the doctor, you're
still supposed to wear a mask, at least in

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.180
the Northeast.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.299
But we are starting to see some things happen
again.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:11.600
Philadelphia will restore its indoor mask
mandate, The Associated Press reporting confirmed

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.890
COVID cases up more than 50 percent in 10
days.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:20.390
That's a predetermined threshold where the
city says masks go back on indoors.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.340
This is being driven by the bay to sub variant
of Akron.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.299
On the original Akron was Bay one.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:30.780
Bay two is this sub variant of Akron.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:36.869
U.S. State Department orders all non-emergency
government staff in Shanghai, China, to leave

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:40.360
as COVID surges.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:44.079
However, the Chinese Foreign Ministry is not
pleased with this.

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:49.539
On Saturday, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson
Zhao Lijian said the US characterization of

00:01:49.539 --> 00:01:56.080
China's COVID policy was a groundless accusation
and that the Chinese side has assisted foreign

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.270
diplomats and consular staff on COVID related
issues.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:06.119
This is in response to the U.S. State Department
warning about the arbitrary enforcement of

00:02:06.119 --> 00:02:13.150
local laws universities reinstating mask mandates
amid COVID surge.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:18.320
The American University announced Monday it's
putting a mask mandate back on in D.C., Columbia,

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:23.430
Georgetown, Johns Hopkins Rice Universities
are also doing this the reason the highly

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:27.710
transmissible be to sub variant.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:32.070
An average of more than 31000 new COVID cases
across the country.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.870
COVID could be surging in the U.S., and we
might not even know about it.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:39.250
This is also an important issue, and I know
a lot of people are sick of hearing about

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.250
this.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:44.380
We know that there is less testing going on.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:49.520
We also know that a lot of the home testing
is not being reported to authorities, so a

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.590
lot of people.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:55.060
This started to be an issue during the first
immigrant wave in December.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:03:00.540
It's an even bigger issue now where increasingly
a lot of people are testing at home testing

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:05.470
positive and then they throw the test out
and they go, I'm positive, and that's it.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:08.800
That doesn't show up in the numbers anywhere.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.830
Not not to, you know, I'm not.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.170
I have no reason to think Sam Seder is doing
this.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.820
But we sadly learned yesterday that our friend
Sam Seder from the majority report has tested

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:18.820
positive.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.500
He's had a bunch of different negative tests,
didn't feel well.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.220
Now he's positive.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.680
I don't know what type of a test that was,
but the point I'm making is without accusing

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.910
Sam of anything.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:33.410
If Sam's eventual positive test was a home
test that's not automatically counted anywhere

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:40.400
unless Sam reports it and because of the decrease
decrease not only in people seeking tests,

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:46.590
but also the decrease in some of these municipal
and federal testing sites, we we just know

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:51.400
we're almost certainly not capturing all of
the cases that are going on.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.040
So what's going to happen?

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.040
I don't know.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:04:02.430
I am convinced that the threshold for people
going back into a cautious state is much higher,

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.320
much, much higher than it was before.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:10.680
And what I mean by that is a slight increase
in cases and deaths at this point for social

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.970
reasons is not going to kind of drive us back.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:19.879
In terms of our precautions, I think people
are much more comfortable accepting a certain

00:04:19.879 --> 00:04:20.879
level of risk.

00:04:20.879 --> 00:04:21.879
I'm not immune to that.

00:04:21.879 --> 00:04:23.800
I went to Las Vegas last week.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.039
I there were there was not a mask in sight.

00:04:26.039 --> 00:04:30.229
I was around thousands of people and thankfully
I didn't.

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:31.250
I didn't get sick.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:35.980
And you know, when I got back, I didn't see
people for four days until I really knew I

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:37.080
was in the clear.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.229
But would I have done that at a previous time?

00:04:39.229 --> 00:04:40.349
You know, probably not.

00:04:40.349 --> 00:04:42.550
At the same time, the numbers look a lot better.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:45.180
So we're going to have to see what happens.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.610
I think you will absolutely see.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:55.470
A much more stark difference between states,
as in all likelihood, cases continue to rise

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:59.610
and eventually hospitalizations do as well.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.740
Let me know your perspective on this.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:02.780
Let me know what you're doing.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.990
Let me know what you're seeing in your state.

